course: dictionary
lesson: 7371
title: Plentiful and its clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Plentiful means there is a lot of something, more than enough. When something is plentiful, you can find it easily. You can hunt for a plentiful food, but a scarce food is hard to find.
explain: Look at the words around plentiful to check its meaning. «They lay more eggs when lemmings are plentiful.» The eggs and lemmings show that the lemmings are in good supply, so the owls have plenty to eat. Try your meaning in the sentence: «they lay more eggs when there is more than enough lemmings» still makes sense.
explain: Scientists and geographers use plentiful about food, water and animals. «Most birds nest in spring, when insects are most plentiful.» In spring, there are lots of insects for the chicks to eat. Plentiful can also appear in stories, such as a plentiful harvest, which means a big, good crop.
fact: Plentiful means there is a lot of something, more than enough.
fact: Plentiful is an adjective, and its forms are plentiful, more plentiful and most plentiful.
fact: The opposite of plentiful is scarce, which means hard to find.
fact: «Mice numbers explode when food is plentiful» because mice have many babies when there is plenty to eat.
fact: Phrases you will meet include plentiful supply and plentiful food.
exercise: «They lay more eggs when lemmings are plentiful.» What does plentiful mean here? | Hard to find | Far away | *There is a lot, more than enough | Very small
exercise: «Most birds nest in spring, when insects are most plentiful.» In spring, what are the insects like? | Hidden under the ground | Gone away for the winter | *There are lots of them for the chicks to eat | Too big to catch
exercise: Which word is the opposite of plentiful? | *Scarce | Abundant | Full | Ample
test: «Numbers explode when food is plentiful.» Why do mouse numbers grow fast, according to this? | Food is hard to find | *There is plenty of food | Mice stop eating | Owls have all left
test: Plentiful is most like which word? | Scarce | *Abundant | Rare | Empty
exam: Which sentence uses plentiful correctly? | The shop was plentiful and had only one apple left. | The desert was plentiful with rain, so nothing grew. | *The harvest was plentiful this year, so the barn was full.
